bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, 0, "At device scale k > 1 the pen after an inline auto-width <button> is taken from the button's device-snapped width (inline_item_width_err_milli: box_device_extra_w_at(c) x 1000 / k); Chrome 159 starts the next item at the button's LayoutUnit width (label advance rounded up to 1/64 device px, plus padding and border). The origin of the text that follows is therefore off by a fraction of a device px, and its glyphs that sit on a quarter-device-px tie take either phase depending on sub-milli changes upstream."
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, 1, "Seen on catalog forms-media at k=4: <button>Exercise controls</button> <output>Not exercised</output>. Band y=1360..1440 device px against Chrome: 1526 mismatching px at 199527f4aef, 1947 with the inline item LayoutUnit ceil (the space item after the button went from 4445 to 4446 milli-px, true value 4445.3125). The page stays at 0.05."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: text after an inline button at k > 1 starts from the button's device-snapped width, not its LayoutUnit width", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl, 1832, "catalog forms-media at --device-scale 4, rows 1360..1440 (Not exercised)", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 inline-ceil lane: found while measuring the item ceil. Not measured in Chrome: the button's getBoundingClientRect width at k=4. Fix sketch: carry the button's exact LayoutUnit width (label width_q20 at the device font size) past it instead of the device-snapped box."
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 button-label-cluster lane: Chrome 159 measured: <button>Exercise controls</button> is 119.5078 at k=4 vs 119.4844 at k=1, the <output> after it at 123.9531 / 123.9375 (a 5-button chain puts it at 401.9219 / 401.875). The premise (box_device_extra_w) is stale: inline_item_width_err_milli takes the button branch first; the real cause was inline_button_width_err_milli using the k=1 label width at k>1. Fix: at k>1 it uses form_control_label_width_milli_px (device-shaped LayoutUnit). Column-level ink was already right on base; the follower's dark-run starts (green < 128, device x >= 495) on rows 50..79 were not: base 30/30 rows differ from Chrome, lane 4/30 (y66 y67 y72 y74). Pixel mismatch (>16 levels) in the band: 801 -> 51 (Exercise controls + output), 3990 -> 190 (5-button chain), 2157 -> 123 (input then button). Red->green: test/01_unit/browser_engine/button_input_device_width_chrome159_spec.spl AC-5 (rows 53, 57, 60, 64); AC-4 pins the k=1/k=4 columns."
    web_render_k4_button_follower_pen_from_device_width_2026-11-28, 2, "2026-11-28 rebase onto release/1.0.0 0829e113e88: upstream 5358ad442c6 made _lay_flex_item_max_content_width_inner ceil every #text run (resolved_font_width_milli + 999), which also ceils a <button> label, so every auto button grew 1 px and its fraction was counted twice with the lane's pen error. On the new base alone button_follower_device_width_chrome159_spec is 1/3 and button_input_device_width_chrome159_spec 0/5 (k=1 Exercise controls button 119 px, Chrome 118). A lane-side <button>-parent skip fixed it; a06f1b1b485 (#12400) then narrowed the ceil to row-flex text children, which covers the button case, so the skip was dropped on the rebase onto b90960cacd7 (both specs 3/3 and 5/5 there without it)."

